[{:db/id "q-237438/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "db112308-76e2-59ee-a782-d3af4c5c73c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-237438/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f80d8a3c-fc64-51cd-b4fe-2ae93b210522" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-237438/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-237438/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-237438" :question/id #uuid "9fb3c079-a60e-5bda-bfec-324752a909a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-237438" :question/problem "If ${a}_{n+2}={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n}$ with ${a}_{1}=0$ and ${a}_{2}=3,$ then ${a}_{3}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1+2} & ={a}_{1+1}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =3+0 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-237438/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d4a21cd-bd8d-5572-b932-76875827170a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-237438"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34325"] :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{450}^{∘}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$\n\n- $-{450}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}=-90$\n\n- $-{450}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={270}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${270}^{∘}$ is coterminal with $-{450}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13939908/assets/35b9783c9ac87b0a8d177e7bdf340b48513146404b7c768a8532da59b6ec7948.png)\n\nWe see that ${270}^{∘}$ lies between quadrants III and IV. Therefore, $-{450}^{∘}$ also lies between these quadrants." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-3526"] :question/worked-solution "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{2a{b}^{2}}{b{c}^{3}}÷\\frac{8{a}^{3}}{7{c}^{4}},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2a{b}^{2}}{b{c}^{3}}÷\\frac{8{a}^{3}}{7{c}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2a{b}^{2}}{b{c}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{7{c}^{4}}{8{a}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2ab\\cdot b}{b{c}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{7c\\cdot {c}^{3}}{4\\cdot 2a\\cdot {a}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2a}b\\cdot \\cancel{b}}{\\cancel{b}\\cancel{{c}^{3}}}\\cdot \\frac{7c\\cdot \\cancel{{c}^{3}}}{4\\cdot \\cancel{2a}\\cdot {a}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7bc}{4{a}^{2}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-118944/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "e40a6195-e0a6-5569-962b-194638c1b2ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118944/selection/efedb545849c1303b8db7ef0cb9b831e3ce01e9a3740f1aba4be27d5520a3499" :answer/id #uuid "6b70beb1-4d50-5923-a65b-f63e167fe831" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118944/selection/add48b243ebaf46eba7641661c03d006608a5acdecbbc38b771c9f737352650c" :answer/id #uuid "0e71e43a-0165-58ba-861e-1e7ac75f1539" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118944/selection/e9b0fcc914cbb593541eab0f5a07d912a354e5fbae56d539c891226a98a1af97" :answer/id #uuid "64137b70-d0e1-5f89-afa3-14159ebf7acc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118944/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "6789bb35-fc2a-529d-89ea-8706539aeccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118944/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2a37dcf-9eee-593f-b167-d4ee34dd3a0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-118944/selection/efedb545849c1303b8db7ef0cb9b831e3ce01e9a3740f1aba4be27d5520a3499" :answer-field/choices ["q-118944/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-118944/selection/efedb545849c1303b8db7ef0cb9b831e3ce01e9a3740f1aba4be27d5520a3499" "q-118944/selection/add48b243ebaf46eba7641661c03d006608a5acdecbbc38b771c9f737352650c" "q-118944/selection/e9b0fcc914cbb593541eab0f5a07d912a354e5fbae56d539c891226a98a1af97" "q-118944/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118944" :question/id #uuid "3329b56b-ec4b-5fc6-8723-d1077c57a901" :question/math-academy-id "q-118944" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(-3s,-4s,7s)$ and $B(s,-6s,3s).$ Given that the distance between $A$ and $B$ is $54,$ find the possible values of $s.$" :question/worked-solution "The distance $d$ between two points $A({x}_{1},{y}_{1},{z}_{1})$ and $B({x}_{2},{y}_{2},{z}_{2})$ is given by\n\n$$\nd=\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $A{{(-3s,-4s,7s)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{, }{y}_{1}\\text{, }{z}_{1}\\text{)}}$ and $B{{(s,-6s,3s)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{, }{y}_{2}\\text{, }{z}_{2}\\text{)}}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(s-(-3s))^{2}+(-6s-(-4s))^{2}+(3s-7s)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4s)^{2}+(-2s)^{2}+(-4s)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{s}^{2}+4{s}^{2}+16{s}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{s}^{2}} \\\\  & =6\\,|s|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $d=54,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\,|s| & =54 \\\\ |s| & =9 \\\\ s & =\\pm 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-118944/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4e178c7-bdb4-5139-a20c-3e17de51ee11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118944"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288779/selection/b78cefa051ec62e42babb0396ce415bc1c6b03c29d281d68224ab0312a503d34" :answer/id #uuid "12fa5be9-1ba2-562a-b62c-04e01dad2d90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288779/selection/2ebc133599183e5fdb5b6248a8ea00bdd0440ff336252ee383591a8699a758ca" :answer/id #uuid "74be56fe-6024-5e32-bb17-f6bb442cdfa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288779/selection/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" :answer/id #uuid "2e6ca8d9-e8dd-57be-846f-25ff22488b22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288779/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "84d1f0c9-4e7e-5f5c-90bd-dbf09292e16a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288779/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "15a875f2-d2d5-5c06-9198-8435fb0d4aff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288779/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "11504366-ff1e-5f73-a407-cb0484718acb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-288779/selection/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" :answer-field/choices ["q-288779/selection/b78cefa051ec62e42babb0396ce415bc1c6b03c29d281d68224ab0312a503d34" "q-288779/selection/2ebc133599183e5fdb5b6248a8ea00bdd0440ff336252ee383591a8699a758ca" "q-288779/selection/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" "q-288779/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" "q-288779/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288779" :question/id #uuid "70cecb06-4a85-561a-ae02-e92e4d923c8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-288779" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic equation\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}+8x-1=0.\n$$\n\n**Without** solving the equation, determine the sum of its solutions." :question/worked-solution "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nFor the given quadratic equation, we have\n\n$$\na=3,\\,b=8,\\,c=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the solutions is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{b}{a} & =-\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288779/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03456ac4-5798-56cc-8c14-0a645b2e232e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288779"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-14147"] :question/worked-solution "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial:\n\n- The constant term is $-2,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm 2.$\n\n- The leading coefficient is $2,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm 2.$\n\nFirst, we list out all the possibilities for the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm \\frac{1}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{2}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the fractions to lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ \\pm 2, & \\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that some potential roots are duplicates (shown above in red). Removing these duplicates, and listing those remaining in order from least to greatest in absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm 2.\n$$\n\nThis makes a total of $6$ potential roots. (Remember that each $\\pm $ sign accounts for $2$ roots, and $2\\cdot 3=6.$)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-319492/field-1/32dffe5e232b44ab381c99a7958bfad74a47018d0c81eb64fd44a46a751cf9a3" :answer/id #uuid "cdcf49bb-f7e2-5c23-9333-af5c047c56cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319492/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ac20aed-4025-5c62-9c23-22fcb072ca0f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319492/field-1/32dffe5e232b44ab381c99a7958bfad74a47018d0c81eb64fd44a46a751cf9a3" :answer-field/choices ["q-319492/field-1/32dffe5e232b44ab381c99a7958bfad74a47018d0c81eb64fd44a46a751cf9a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319492" :question/id #uuid "18ca621b-aa9c-527c-a411-a69f8c48899c" :question/math-academy-id "q-319492" :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-5+3\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13939908/assets/217fc7ba4c6a6c18d0be184a9d5cc7b0a682ed2bd0da6e284955040643bc2e03.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)<\\pi .$\n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan\\,(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =0.540\\,419…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)=\\pi -0.540\\,419…≈2.60,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/requires-calculator true :question/answer-fields ["q-319492/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "833ac63c-235b-5059-ab7c-56eb1e44d79e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319492"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276793/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c95ceacd-c9bc-5cec-b342-df5855bba0cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276793/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "548003a4-06f8-530b-a264-d0ff9736ac62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276793/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-276793/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276793" :question/id #uuid "fb65edc8-082c-52ff-844e-1ac02a93d381" :question/math-academy-id "q-276793" :question/problem "The function $f(x)=\\frac{5}{kx-1}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5+x}{x}.$ What is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{kx-1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{ky-1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5}{ky-1} \\\\ x(ky-1) & =5 \\\\ kxy-x & =5 \\\\ kxy & =5+x \\\\ y & =\\frac{5+x}{kx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5+x}{kx}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-276793/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcedd9d0-f87c-58b2-9ef1-c9fa0ef2e5c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276793"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
